This is the lifecycle overview, not the exact Bitrise dependency graph. Signing, device-test preparation, security assessment, and distribution ordering follow the approved route/template. Do not infer that every repository publishes to every destination or that all gates run only once.

The required template determines source-branch requirements. The configuration repository has its own review and promotion branches. Do not confuse an application source branch with the branch that authorizes a live provisioning apply.

## 3. Know who performs each action

| Role | Responsibility |
| :--- | :--- |
| Application developer / request author | Prepare the application, verify local readiness, submit a secret-free request, and record the intended source identity. |
| Reviewer / code owner | Review source or configuration changes, validate requested access and template compatibility, and satisfy the applicable branch rules. |
| Platform Engineering | Own provisioning, approved templates, protected credential bindings, platform changes, and recovery from partial applies. |
| Authorized Vela operator | Inspect protected validation/apply results through the approved access path and share sanitized evidence. |
| QA / business tester | Verify the intended application version and report test results and audience access. |
| Application owner / release authority | Own the intended audience, applicable approvals, and authorization to release to the selected destination. |

A workshop facilitator may coordinate these roles, but does not replace protected-branch rules or release authorization. Developers do not need raw signing credentials or manual app-provisioning access to follow the governed enrollment path.

### Access readiness

Before starting a live exercise or first enrollment, confirm:

- You can access the approved application template and its dependency registry instructions.
- You can create or contribute to the intended private application repository.
- You can read the current workflow catalog and submit the configuration request through the approved process.
- Required reviewers and Platform Engineering contacts are identified.
- An authorized operator can inspect Vela results through the approved network/access path.
- You can inspect the relevant Bitrise builds and approved distribution catalog for your role.
- The target account, environment, and audience are explicitly identified.

