## 7. Understand approvals and store boundaries

Required TGRC security approval must be established before UAT or Production deployment under the supplied company policy. Record approval identity and applicability through the approved evidence mechanism; never infer approval from a green compilation result.

Detailed listing metadata, screenshots, public privacy-policy requirements, submission procedures, enterprise installation, and user-entitlement instructions belong in the dedicated **App Store documentation section**.

This CI/CD section covers automated delivery, protected credential integration, approval gates, destination readback, and release evidence. An upload to Google Play testing or TestFlight is not automatically a public production release.

## 8. Stop safely on partial failure

<MermaidZoom title="Unknown external outcome · preserve and reconcile">

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    RESULT{"External operation outcome"}
    SUCCESS["Confirmed success<br/>Record evidence and continue approved dependencies"]
    FAILURE["Confirmed failure or unknown side effect"]
    STOP["Stop affected operation<br/>Preserve app, artifacts, credentials, and completed routes"]
    READ["Authorized read-only reconciliation<br/>Match request, commit, operation identity, and destination state"]
    RECOVERY["Follow reviewed recovery procedure<br/>No blind create, upload, or credential replacement"]
    RESULT -->|"Confirmed"| SUCCESS
    RESULT -->|"Failed / ambiguous"| FAILURE --> STOP --> READ --> RECOVERY
    classDef ok fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#059669,color:#064e3b,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef control fill:#eef2ff,stroke:#6366f1,color:#1e1b4b,stroke-width:1.5px;
    classDef caution fill:#fffbeb,stroke:#d97706,color:#78350f,stroke-width:1.5px;
    class RESULT caution;
    class SUCCESS ok;
    class FAILURE,STOP,READ,RECOVERY control;
```

</MermaidZoom>

The one-write rule prohibits blindly repeating an ambiguous external mutation. Preserve the request revision, protected merge, apply/build identities, correlation identity, exact failed route, and sanitized result. A timeout does not prove that the external service rejected the operation. A single negative readback may also be insufficient to establish absence.

The operator recovery guide defines the permitted reconciliation and any subsequently authorized mutation. The developer's immediate action is to preserve state and escalate with evidence, not improvise a repair.

## 9. Use workshop evidence correctly

The supplied workshop demonstrates application generation, secret-free request submission, validation, promotion, protected apply inspection, and route-by-route distribution checks.

Its historical reference run had a partial outcome: one QA route had confirmed distribution, another had build success followed by distribution-signing failure, and UAT publication was not confirmed. That observation does not establish current platform health or the status of a new application.

The workshop page contains sanitized exercises and dated historical evidence. Do not reuse its existing application identity as a new enrollment request, copy its historical template version as the current approved version, or invent a root cause for the observed failure.

